    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This semi-detached, four-bay, three-storey residence is offered for sale by private treaty. \n\nExtending to approximately 260.26 sq. m (2,801 sq. ft), the eleven-room property dates from the early 1800s and presents a rare opportunity for restoration and renewal, in a prime residential area. \n\nUnoccupied since 1988, the house awaits a purchaser with the vision to restore it to its former grandeur. As a protected structure, this remarkable property offers a unique chance to preserve an important piece of the architectural and cultural heritage of Sligo. The house is noted for its distinctive half-hipped roof and an enclosed rear courtyard. Set in an idyllic location, it combines period character and exceptional potential to become an outstanding family residence.\n"
      },
